.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

const char *json_get_string(const char *json, const char *key,
                            char *buf, size_t bufsize);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Extracts the string value associated with \f[CR]key\f[R] from a JSON
object string.
Searches for the pattern \f[CR]\(dqkey\(dq:\(dqvalue\(dq\f[R] using
\f[CR]strstr(3)\f[R], then copies the unescaped value into
\f[CR]buf\f[R].
.PP
The function handles standard JSON string escapes: \f[CR]\(rs\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(rs\(rs\f[R], \f[CR]\(rs/\f[R], \f[CR]\(rsn\f[R],
\f[CR]\(rsr\f[R], \f[CR]\(rst\f[R], \f[CR]\(rsb\f[R], \f[CR]\(rsf\f[R],
and \f[CR]\(rsuXXXX\f[R] (ASCII range only, codes >= 0x80 are silently
dropped).
.PP
This is a minimal JSON parser designed for the flat JSON objects used in
the bash\-server protocol.
It does not traverse nested objects or arrays.
