.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to \f[CR]buf\f[R] on success (same pointer passed in).
.PP
Returns \f[B]NULL\f[R] if: \- The key is not found in the JSON string.
\- The value associated with the key is not a string (does not start
with \f[CR]\(dq\f[R]).
\- The key name exceeds 253 characters.
\- Unescape fails (malformed escape sequence).
.SH ERRORS
No \f[CR]errno\f[R] is set.
NULL return indicates the key was not found or the value is not a
string.
